          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong graph
            is a collection of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge"} edge
            links a pair of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            %em incidence
            between vertices and edges. There are several variations on the idea, described below.
          %p
            This is the sense of graph in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times B
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph of a function
            for more on this.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            be
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            %strong vertex
            and an element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            an
            = succeed "." do
              %strong edge
            %strong graph
            is given by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            that interprets edges as pairs of vertices. Exactly what this means depends on how one defines ‘mapping that interprets’ and ‘pair’; the possibilities are given below. We will need the following notation:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^2
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with itself, the set of ordered pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y)
              of vertices;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_V
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+subset"} diagonal subset
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
